WEBVTT

00:02.880 --> 00:06.420
Now, I'll announce our soloists.

00:06.970 --> 00:09.480
Third-year, Kuroe Mayu-san.

01:41.660 --> 01:44.630
That concludes all the announcements.

01:44.970 --> 01:47.680
Now, let's continue ensemble practice.

01:47.680 --> 01:50.570
Competition members will 
stay here to rehearse.

01:51.250 --> 01:54.000
Everyone else, please move.

01:59.260 --> 02:00.510
Kumiko-chan.

02:02.530 --> 02:05.620
We can stay in our spots.

02:05.620 --> 02:07.370
You don't have to move, okay?

02:09.260 --> 02:13.020
Kuroe-senpai doesn't mind 
Kumiko-senpai being the one

02:13.020 --> 02:17.200
sitting by the conductor 
even if the soloists swap.

02:17.670 --> 02:19.780
That's what I'm hearing.

02:19.780 --> 02:22.130
No, we should switch.

02:22.440 --> 02:23.240
But...

02:24.780 --> 02:26.560
I told you, remember?

02:26.560 --> 02:29.120
At Kitauji, if you're 
capable, you come first.

02:31.280 --> 02:32.660
Kanade-chan...

02:33.970 --> 02:35.700
I'm fine.

02:36.440 --> 02:39.850
Let me talk to you again 
after practice or something.

02:43.600 --> 02:49.340
<i>We ended up with two 
euphoniums and four tubas.</i>

02:50.270 --> 02:56.970
<i>And the euphonium soloist changed.</i>

02:58.900 --> 03:02.780
<b>Episode 9</b>

02:58.900 --> 03:02.780
<b>Dissonant Tuning</b>

03:07.530 --> 03:14.300
Clarinet, oboe, flute, please end your 
trills at the beginning together.

03:14.300 --> 03:15.290
Yes.

03:15.590 --> 03:18.660
Clarinets, play those tuplets clearly.

03:19.140 --> 03:21.850
Glock, watch out for that entry.

03:21.850 --> 03:23.090
It's your turn to shine.

03:23.090 --> 03:23.870
Yes.

03:30.410 --> 03:33.580
Taki-kun, mind if I say something?

03:34.150 --> 03:35.170
Go ahead.

03:36.650 --> 03:38.020
You know...

03:38.460 --> 03:42.030
You're all really tense this year.

03:42.030 --> 03:44.910
Like, you're completely petrified.

03:44.910 --> 03:46.150
You're stiff.

03:46.150 --> 03:50.770
You could say you're the raccoon 
dogs of Kachikachi-yama.

03:50.770 --> 03:53.530
Why don't you go back to 
your mommy's breasts?

03:55.940 --> 03:59.170
Wait, did I just bomb?

04:00.160 --> 04:01.470
I'm sorry!

04:04.530 --> 04:06.980
That's it. That's the spirit.

04:06.980 --> 04:08.820
Keep your minds loose.

04:09.340 --> 04:13.500
The seniors are probably sick of hearing 
this, but when you play music, you—

04:13.500 --> 04:15.350
You <i>play</i>.

04:15.350 --> 04:16.460
Play music.

04:17.470 --> 04:18.490
Correct?

04:20.800 --> 04:22.600
Do you really get it?

04:25.760 --> 04:27.170
I do.

04:28.090 --> 04:30.280
Well, from the top, once more.

04:34.410 --> 04:35.500
Kumiko-chan!

04:36.960 --> 04:38.360
Kumiko-chan!

04:41.200 --> 04:42.500
Are you okay?

04:44.820 --> 04:46.260
What's up?

04:51.000 --> 04:54.950
Hey, I still think we should switch.

04:56.230 --> 04:58.020
I don't need to play the soli.

04:58.020 --> 05:01.650
I'm begging you, please stop saying that.

05:03.420 --> 05:05.000
S-Sorry.

05:05.840 --> 05:07.840
You don't need to apologize.

05:07.840 --> 05:10.560
I'm really not upset about it.

05:11.400 --> 05:13.300
You're going back to your room, right?

05:13.830 --> 05:15.400
Can I come with you?

05:19.450 --> 05:20.820
I want to take a break.

05:20.820 --> 05:23.060
Is it all right if I'm alone for a bit?

05:27.660 --> 05:30.120
<i>I feel something like anger.</i>

05:30.120 --> 05:32.170
<i>I don't know what it's directed at.</i>

05:32.580 --> 05:34.170
<i>Is it towards me?</i>

05:34.590 --> 05:36.430
<i>Or at Mayu-chan?</i>

05:37.110 --> 05:40.980
<i>Or at something else entirely?</i>

05:42.600 --> 05:44.480
Kumiko-senpai.

05:45.520 --> 05:46.910
Kanade-chan.

05:47.770 --> 05:50.770
You're going to hurt 
yourself walking so fast.

05:52.940 --> 05:54.730
I told you so.

05:54.730 --> 05:56.460
She's terrifying.

05:56.780 --> 05:59.530
She doesn't scare me or anything.

06:00.080 --> 06:03.110
It's not like she did anything.

06:03.910 --> 06:05.540
Even the audition was...

06:07.330 --> 06:08.150
Yes?

06:09.520 --> 06:12.890
Sorry you didn't make the 
cut for the competition.

06:12.890 --> 06:14.670
Isn't that a bit late?

06:15.160 --> 06:20.520
I talked to you hoping you'd 
console me as soon as you saw me.

06:20.520 --> 06:22.310
You were, huh?

06:22.870 --> 06:23.800
Sorry.

06:24.430 --> 06:26.740
Please don't take me seriously.

06:26.740 --> 06:27.920
I'm just kidding.

06:28.520 --> 06:30.000
Besides...

06:30.560 --> 06:32.940
I kind of saw it coming.

06:33.290 --> 06:34.820
You did?

06:35.220 --> 06:39.070
You and Kuroe-senpai can handle 
the euph parts just fine.

06:39.070 --> 06:44.080
Gotou-senpai drops out, and the tubas get 
more members to boost their confidence.

06:44.420 --> 06:46.460
It's just a matter of balance.

06:46.840 --> 06:51.460
You can't add a member without 
taking someone away elsewhere.

06:53.080 --> 06:56.820
I guess I don't need to cheer you up 
if you're <i>that</i> aware of the situation.

06:56.820 --> 06:59.280
I still want you to.

06:59.280 --> 07:03.390
The fact remains that I failed, after all.

07:03.700 --> 07:05.140
This kid's a pain.

07:05.140 --> 07:06.590
You said that out loud.

07:15.520 --> 07:17.920
Taki-sensei's the one to blame.

07:18.250 --> 07:22.920
We could have just settled on four 
tubas from the Prefecturals.

07:23.190 --> 07:25.410
Yet he's just meandering.

07:25.410 --> 07:29.060
I don't think he's trying to meander.

07:30.430 --> 07:32.430
Do you really think so?

07:36.290 --> 07:42.150
I can't shake the feeling that Taki-sensei's 
decision-making this year is off somehow.

07:42.520 --> 07:44.770
Same thing with the soli.

07:44.770 --> 07:49.840
You and Kuroe-senpai are 
almost equally capable.

07:50.630 --> 07:55.600
So he could only have switch soloists 
because his criteria have changed.

07:56.220 --> 08:01.410
I thought it was just that 
Mayu-chan's playing better than me.

08:01.410 --> 08:03.740
Do you seriously think that?

08:04.030 --> 08:07.930
That one of you has gotten definitively 
better since the Prefecturals?

08:08.330 --> 08:13.670
The third-years seem to have blind faith 
in everything Taki-sensei decides.

08:14.250 --> 08:16.890
I don't think we're following him blindly.

08:20.390 --> 08:22.240
All right, then.

08:23.090 --> 08:24.350
You're satisfied?

08:25.440 --> 08:26.380
Yes.

08:27.730 --> 08:30.100
I'm just kinda venting.

08:31.960 --> 08:33.990
Here we go.

08:34.380 --> 08:36.330
Ready, and...

08:42.260 --> 08:44.740
Could you please help me out next?

08:46.330 --> 08:47.260
With what?

08:48.640 --> 08:51.870
N-Nothing. Never mind.

08:51.870 --> 08:56.280
Hey, I'm rooting for you, President.

08:56.280 --> 08:58.230
Uh-huh, thanks.

09:04.580 --> 09:05.720
Long day, huh?

09:07.040 --> 09:09.650
Seriously long day.

09:09.650 --> 09:11.740
I'm exhausted.

09:12.350 --> 09:17.240
I still think this is for the 
best, despite the outcome.

09:20.990 --> 09:22.450
I'm sorry.

09:22.920 --> 09:26.910
I was hoping to play the soli with you.

09:27.400 --> 09:29.450
We still have the Nationals.

09:29.870 --> 09:32.310
Yeah... but...

09:34.520 --> 09:39.590
Why do you think I wasn't 
chosen to play the soli?

09:41.600 --> 09:44.710
I haven't heard the 
auditions, so I can't say.

09:45.870 --> 09:50.790
But it's true that Kuroe-san 
is as talented as you are.

09:52.230 --> 09:55.190
Besides that, I think it's just 
what Taki-sensei decided.

09:55.590 --> 09:56.560
Yeah?

09:57.810 --> 10:01.110
I trust in Taki-sensei's decisions.

10:01.110 --> 10:04.440
So I accept this result just the same.

10:06.350 --> 10:09.800
I still can't believe Kanade wasn't 
picked for the competition.

10:09.800 --> 10:12.420
Do we even need four tubas?

10:12.420 --> 10:13.530
Right?

10:13.530 --> 10:15.470
I was thinking about that, too.

10:16.640 --> 10:18.240
You there.

10:18.740 --> 10:20.780
I have something important 
to talk to you about.

10:20.780 --> 10:23.740
Please come to the rec room at 10 PM.

10:23.740 --> 10:26.280
No, we were just...

10:28.090 --> 10:29.220
Right...

10:33.630 --> 10:34.870
Umm...

10:34.870 --> 10:35.980
Reina-san?

10:35.980 --> 10:36.950
What?

10:37.360 --> 10:40.190
Are you going to scold them?

10:40.550 --> 10:42.450
I'm warning them.

10:42.450 --> 10:46.730
We can't allow people to talk like 
that about the club advisor.

10:47.120 --> 10:50.120
I think it's just a mild gripe.

10:50.390 --> 10:54.990
The members will lose trust 
in Taki-sensei if we allow it.

10:55.410 --> 10:57.840
That will affect our performance.

10:58.220 --> 11:01.440
As the drum major, I can't allow that.

11:02.050 --> 11:03.530
But you know...

11:03.530 --> 11:04.460
Most of all...

11:06.280 --> 11:10.400
Taki-sensei didn't do anything wrong.

11:12.060 --> 11:12.780
Here.

11:13.140 --> 11:14.400
Senko hanabi sparklers.

11:14.870 --> 11:16.030
Come on.

11:16.730 --> 11:18.070
Thanks.

11:21.630 --> 11:24.870
Did you do fireworks at camp at Seira, too?

11:24.870 --> 11:26.100
Yeah.

11:26.100 --> 11:28.240
I think we did tests of courage, too.

11:29.040 --> 11:32.150
Our seniors would dress 
up as ghosts and stuff.

11:32.150 --> 11:33.970
Wow.

11:36.780 --> 11:41.290
Everyone's angry, aren't they?

11:41.290 --> 11:43.060
Because I ended up with the soli.

11:43.500 --> 11:46.060
I don't think they're angry.

11:46.670 --> 11:48.510
Even though there might be a lot of people

11:48.510 --> 11:51.200
rooting for Kumiko-chan 
since she's the president.

11:52.640 --> 11:53.770
I'm sure.

11:54.930 --> 11:58.110
But hearing you play, I've always thought...

11:58.420 --> 12:01.190
That I wouldn't be surprised 
if you were chosen.

12:02.450 --> 12:03.750
Really?

12:03.750 --> 12:05.890
So I'm relieved.

12:05.890 --> 12:09.630
Taki-sensei isn't playing favorites for 
the presidents or executives or anything.

12:09.630 --> 12:12.200
He's really deciding based 
on how people sound.

12:14.330 --> 12:16.000
It's just getting started.

12:17.700 --> 12:19.020
Oh, look.

12:30.030 --> 12:32.830
I think I still have the 
smell of fireworks on me.

12:32.830 --> 12:34.240
I think you're fine.

12:34.520 --> 12:36.850
Oh, s-sorry...

12:37.340 --> 12:38.610
What's up?

12:39.040 --> 12:41.240
Well, I just...

12:41.950 --> 12:43.450
What do you want?

12:43.450 --> 12:45.350
I said it's nothing.

12:45.660 --> 12:49.900
What are you doing, worrying 
our underclassmen like that?

12:49.900 --> 12:52.720
It's everyone else that's worrying too much.

12:52.720 --> 12:54.610
What, are you being cranky?

12:55.260 --> 12:56.460
Not really.

12:57.650 --> 13:02.390
If you're not going to tell me 
why, at least suffer in silence.

13:01.510 --> 13:03.370
Are you happy with this?

13:03.910 --> 13:05.130
With the audition?

13:06.500 --> 13:10.820
I'm not convinced you're worse than Kuroe.

13:12.260 --> 13:14.390
Is that really why...

13:14.390 --> 13:16.890
Not necessarily.

13:17.720 --> 13:24.400
But I just can't bring myself to agree 
with the results like I could before.

13:25.250 --> 13:26.640
Like...

13:27.660 --> 13:29.780
The result is the result, but...

13:30.690 --> 13:37.410
The way you got swapped 
out out of the blue...

13:38.170 --> 13:39.840
It just doesn't feel right.

13:41.680 --> 13:43.520
Snap out of it.

13:43.520 --> 13:46.820
Mayu-chan was better than me. 
That's why she got the part.

13:47.450 --> 13:49.380
I'm satisfied with that.

13:50.470 --> 13:51.800
You really are?

13:51.800 --> 13:53.260
Of course.

13:53.260 --> 13:55.520
So stop worrying about silly things.

13:55.520 --> 13:57.240
Get a grip!

13:57.240 --> 13:59.400
You're the vice president!

14:08.080 --> 14:09.400
Kumiko-chan.

14:14.270 --> 14:14.830
I still...

14:14.830 --> 14:19.220
You were chosen, so I want you to play 
properly at the Kansai competition.

14:19.620 --> 14:24.770
I want you to work your hardest to make 
sure Kitauji wins gold at Nationals.

14:26.110 --> 14:28.730
That's all I have to say.

14:31.060 --> 14:31.840
Okay.

14:32.410 --> 14:33.390
Got it.

14:37.060 --> 14:44.770
<i>And thus, with unresolved frustrations, 
the three-day camp came to an end.</i>

14:52.730 --> 14:56.070
Okay, anything else we need to go over?

14:53.490 --> 14:55.120
Leader meeting

14:56.500 --> 14:57.610
Yes.

14:58.160 --> 15:04.550
The people who didn't make the audition 
the other day are pretty depressed.

15:04.550 --> 15:06.390
Yeah, of course.

15:06.390 --> 15:09.590
I'm hoping we can remind them 
there's still next time.

15:09.590 --> 15:13.190
We're not sure about that either, though.

15:13.610 --> 15:17.350
The question is: "How we can 
keep them encouraged?"

15:17.790 --> 15:20.300
I think we can leave them behind
 if they aren't taking it seriously.

15:20.300 --> 15:22.220
That's not an answer.

15:22.220 --> 15:24.580
We still need to think 
about next year onward.

15:27.740 --> 15:30.870
Some problems will resolve 
themselves with time.

15:30.870 --> 15:34.370
Just keep an eye on them and talk 
to them when it seems right to.

15:34.370 --> 15:35.660
Got it.

15:36.340 --> 15:39.110
Although... It's not like we have 
much energy to spare, either.

15:39.590 --> 15:44.020
Even if we do make Nationals, 
the thought of auditioning again...

15:44.020 --> 15:47.840
The mood in the club isn't as light 
as it was last year, either.

15:49.860 --> 15:53.560
I think it's good that we 
have some sense of urgency.

15:54.120 --> 15:57.880
We're playing the repertoire 
better than we were last year.

15:58.160 --> 16:01.380
I get that, but...

16:02.330 --> 16:03.890
That's not what I'm saying.

16:03.890 --> 16:08.170
I'm saying we aren't achieving anything 
by suffocating them even more.

16:08.170 --> 16:09.770
"Suffocating them"?

16:09.770 --> 16:12.620
I'm talking common sense here.

16:12.620 --> 16:16.270
Maybe it's common sense to you, but...

16:16.740 --> 16:19.300
It's not about me.

16:19.300 --> 16:21.810
If we're really aiming for 
gold at the Nationals,

16:21.810 --> 16:24.420
we need to be willing to 
<i>make</i> this our common sense.

16:24.720 --> 16:28.410
We didn't win last year or the year before.

16:28.410 --> 16:30.620
We need to make some changes.

16:30.620 --> 16:31.270
Am I wrong?

16:32.390 --> 16:34.310
You're absolutely right.

16:36.510 --> 16:37.960
What do you think, Kumiko?

16:42.800 --> 16:45.520
I think you're right, Reina.

16:53.820 --> 16:54.820
Sorry.

16:54.820 --> 16:55.450
Hm?

16:55.450 --> 16:56.900
Oh, no.

16:56.900 --> 16:59.290
I get where you're coming from, too.

16:59.290 --> 17:00.180
No...

17:00.910 --> 17:02.850
About what happened at camp.

17:03.360 --> 17:04.830
That was childish of me.

17:09.240 --> 17:12.180
I never even thought of you as 
being grown-up to begin with.

17:15.260 --> 17:16.450
Oh.

17:20.410 --> 17:23.220
The wind is so lukewarm.

17:23.670 --> 17:26.090
It's still hot.

17:26.640 --> 17:28.460
But man...

17:28.460 --> 17:33.110
Rehearsal is even more tense 
now, without Hashimocchan.

17:33.470 --> 17:37.060
There's, like, a heavy exhaustion 
that hits you after it's over.

17:37.060 --> 17:38.450
W-Well...

17:38.450 --> 17:40.810
The Kansai competition's coming up.

17:40.810 --> 17:43.000
I get that, but...

17:43.000 --> 17:46.520
It's not the kind of misery where 
you aren't playing too well.

17:46.520 --> 17:48.040
I get it.

17:48.670 --> 17:52.810
Maybe we shouldn't talk about 
that kind of thing right now.

17:52.810 --> 17:53.950
Why not?

17:53.950 --> 17:58.130
How does Kitauji look from your 
perspective right now, Kumiko-chan?

17:58.130 --> 18:01.490
Huh? Um...

18:01.490 --> 18:05.350
I mean, I know there's a 
lot going on right now.

18:05.350 --> 18:09.940
But it's our first time 
doing auditions like this.

18:10.750 --> 18:13.610
So it was harder than you expected?

18:15.750 --> 18:19.000
A little bit.

18:19.300 --> 18:23.120
I think the biggest reason 
is Taki-sensei, though.

18:24.130 --> 18:27.760
I think he's changed too much 
since the Prefecturals.

18:27.760 --> 18:34.270
That's what Taki-sensei decided is right, 
though, so I'm sure he has his reasons.

18:34.270 --> 18:39.360
But I think you and Mayu-chan 
are equally capable.

18:39.360 --> 18:43.530
So I think he should have chosen you.

18:43.530 --> 18:46.260
So you're on that side, huh?

18:46.260 --> 18:47.800
I'm not picking sides.

18:47.800 --> 18:50.440
I just think that would have 
kept the peace within the club.

18:50.880 --> 18:53.180
It's made the club members anxious,

18:53.180 --> 18:56.890
and Mayu-chan can't feel comfortable 
having to replace you, either.

18:56.890 --> 19:00.330
So you do think she's uncomfortable?

19:00.330 --> 19:03.890
I haven't asked her directly, but...

19:03.890 --> 19:08.030
Then again, I don't think 
auditions would make any sense

19:08.030 --> 19:10.120
if you were worried about 
that kind of thing.

19:10.460 --> 19:14.000
I get that, but...

19:15.790 --> 19:20.620
Personally, I think she was 
chosen purely based on skill.

19:21.130 --> 19:23.600
That's why I was satisfied 
with the outcome last year,

19:23.600 --> 19:25.510
and it motivated me for this year.

19:34.270 --> 19:36.780
I'm on my way

19:34.270 --> 19:36.780
I'm leaving

19:39.440 --> 19:40.560
Reina!

19:41.140 --> 19:42.110
Sorry.

19:43.770 --> 19:45.000
Kumiko...

19:45.600 --> 19:47.980
What do you think about 
Taki-sensei's decisions?

19:49.490 --> 19:52.290
Do you think he's making a mistake?

19:55.920 --> 19:57.250
You do, don't you?

19:57.560 --> 19:59.580
No, it's not that.

19:59.580 --> 20:06.510
It's just that, there are a lot of decisions 
that I don't understand, unlike last year.

20:06.860 --> 20:10.100
Question that, and everything falls apart.

20:10.770 --> 20:14.520
Following the instructor's policies 
is fundamental, isn't it?

20:14.520 --> 20:16.600
Everyone <i>is</i> following him.

20:16.600 --> 20:19.510
But you can't expect people who 
don't understand his policies

20:19.510 --> 20:22.890
to just ignore their concerns and 
follow him blindly, can you?

20:23.750 --> 20:27.790
That's not because they don't understand.

20:27.790 --> 20:32.230
Most of them are just ignoring 
their lack of effort and whining

20:32.230 --> 20:34.790
and complaining that things 
aren't going their way.

20:50.370 --> 20:54.130
I don't think that's true.

20:54.880 --> 20:56.150
Kumiko...

20:56.150 --> 20:59.420
So many people have concerns.

20:59.420 --> 21:01.710
As the president, I can't just dismiss them.

21:02.360 --> 21:10.550
I'd be lying if I said I fully trust 
Taki-sensei on this latest matter.

21:11.570 --> 21:13.220
Do you really mean that?

21:14.940 --> 21:15.760
Yes.

21:16.450 --> 21:19.410
Then you're a failure of a president.

21:32.760 --> 21:37.520
<i>I doubt we'd go to school together tomorrow</i>

21:37.520 --> 21:39.920
<i>or talk to each other for 
the foreseeable future.</i>

21:41.000 --> 21:46.220
<i>At the same time, I was somehow 
glad we didn't say goodbye.</i>

21:46.660 --> 21:50.010
<i>Part of me was trying to pretend 
it wasn't really happening.</i>

21:51.230 --> 21:52.500
I'm home.

21:52.500 --> 21:54.230
Welcome home.

21:56.460 --> 21:58.860
What, did you get in a fight or something?

22:01.050 --> 22:02.490
You look devastated.

22:07.090 --> 22:08.390
No kidding.

22:09.660 --> 22:10.760
Sorry?

22:12.010 --> 22:13.260
Never mind.

22:20.740 --> 22:25.810
<i>Local train on track number two. The doors 
are now closing. Please stand clear.</i>

22:45.570 --> 22:47.820
You're the first one here, Oumae-san.

22:48.340 --> 22:51.500
Kousaka-san isn't with you today, huh?

22:52.210 --> 22:54.810
It's not like we're always together.

22:55.690 --> 22:56.830
I see.

22:58.820 --> 23:00.600
Please and thank you.

23:06.900 --> 23:07.820
Sensei...

23:08.890 --> 23:10.070
What is it?

23:15.380 --> 23:17.730
There's something I want to ask you.

23:20.240 --> 23:24.420
<i>And the next piece begins.</i>

23:21.960 --> 23:25.960
<b>To be continued</b>
